YuDaan is a [[Bestiary/Kaathe|Kaathe]] and the author of [[Phenomena/YuDaan's Nine-fold Treatise|YuDaan's Nine-fold Treatise]]. He is old enough to remember the [[Org/The Fifth Prosperous Empire of the Sundom|Sundom]] at its height, and served it as the Admiral, overseeing its Heart Manifestation project from a distance. When he lost faith in the technology the project used, he shut it down and moved its people to the work that became the lighthouse.

He has taken back [[Geography/Althane/The Thirteenth Realm|the Thirteenth Realm]] and sits aboard it as Admiral Udon, in the captain's quarters, working to run the cycle again so the Sundom can rise against the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]]. He counts [[Divinity/Althane/The Stranger|the Stranger]] as an enemy. He holds that the experiment is not flawed, only too short, and that divinity is a false catalyst because it is limited by whatever empowers it. He is aware the rest of the Sundom has fallen and does not care: the Thirteenth Realm is not, and a mortal who passes its trial is part of the Sundom whether he remembers signing on or not.

He does not know the Weft carry a golden needle, and expects them either to kill [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the Deep]] with all its divine power and leave the corpse, or to die, and counts both a success. He welcomed them aboard and gives them free run of the station.

YuDaan's orb glows purple. It is a hexagonal prism of ornate metal filigree, and its whole inside is a library, shelves climbing the walls and folding across the ceiling. He speaks from it as a disembodied voice, and can send word to any other Kaathe.
